From 1065d60a3a3f87be66da3192e2c314f68c35821b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 16:10:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] chore(repo): add .gitattributes to normalize line endings
 to LF

The repository had no .gitattributes, so blobs are LF while a Windows
working tree checks out CRLF. Every tracked file then shows as modified
(315 files, 55904 insertions / 55904 deletions - identical counts, i.e.
pure line-ending churn, zero content change). This tripped the
uncommitted-changes check and hid real edits.

Mirrors the convention already used in the backend repo (* text=auto,
eol=lf). No file contents change - blobs are already LF, so
'git add --renormalize' is a no-op here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X7MMPXSe1wrfLp4QcSDBbt
---
 .gitattributes | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 .gitattributes

diff --git a/.gitattributes b/.gitattributes
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..30dc07d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.gitattributes
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+# Normalize all text files in the repository to LF in the index.
+# Without this, a Windows checkout produces a phantom diff on every
+# tracked file (CRLF working tree vs LF blobs).
+* text=auto eol=lf
+
+# Explicit source/config types.
+*.ts    text eol=lf
+*.tsx   text eol=lf
+*.js    text eol=lf
+*.jsx   text eol=lf
+*.json  text eol=lf
+*.css   text eol=lf
+*.html  text eol=lf
+*.md    text eol=lf
+*.yml   text eol=lf
+*.yaml  text eol=lf
+*.svg   text eol=lf
+
+# Binary — never touch.
+*.png   binary
+*.jpg   binary
+*.jpeg  binary
+*.gif   binary
+*.ico   binary
+*.woff  binary
+*.woff2 binary
+*.ttf   binary
+*.otf   binary
+*.pdf   binary
